WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.855
- Good morning, Believe Nation, it's Evan.

00:00:01.855 --> 00:00:04.639
My one word is believe,
and I believe in people

00:00:04.639 --> 00:00:07.041
more than they believe in
themselves, and my sincere

00:00:07.041 --> 00:00:10.297
hope is that if you see in
yourself, what I see in you,

00:00:10.297 --> 00:00:12.302
you'll be able to change the planet.

00:00:12.302 --> 00:00:14.216
So to help you on your
journey, today's message

00:00:14.216 --> 00:00:15.966
is execute your idea.

00:00:16.823 --> 00:00:18.613
Over to you, Jeff Basos.

00:00:18.613 --> 00:00:20.358
(rooster crowing)

00:00:20.358 --> 00:00:23.503
(upbeat music)
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:23.503 --> 00:00:26.199
♫ Entspresso keep me goin'

00:00:26.199 --> 00:00:30.438
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:30.438 --> 00:00:33.453
- So, it's easy to have ideas.

00:00:33.453 --> 00:00:37.460
It's very hard to turn an idea
into a successful product.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:39.719
There are a lot of steps
in between and it takes

00:00:39.719 --> 00:00:42.521
persistence, relentlessness.

00:00:42.521 --> 00:00:45.282
So I always tell people who are, you know,

00:00:45.282 --> 00:00:47.249
who think they want to be entrepreneurs,

00:00:47.249 --> 00:00:49.832
it's, you need a combination of

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.234
stubborn relentlessness

00:00:54.234 --> 00:00:55.567
and flexibility.

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.478
And you have to know when to be which.

00:00:58.478 --> 00:01:01.523
And basically, you need to
be stubborn on your vision

00:01:01.523 --> 00:01:04.360
because otherwise it will
be too easy to give up.

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:07.810
But, you need to be very
flexible on the details,

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:10.444
because as you go along
pursuing your vision,

00:01:10.444 --> 00:01:13.252
you'll find that some of your
preconceptions were wrong.

00:01:13.252 --> 00:01:16.211
And you're going to need to be
able to change those things.

00:01:16.211 --> 00:01:20.649
So, I think, taking an idea
successfully all the way

00:01:20.649 --> 00:01:22.867
to the market, and turning
it into a real product

00:01:22.867 --> 00:01:24.828
that people care about
and that really improves

00:01:24.828 --> 00:01:27.952
people's lives, is a lot of hard work.

00:01:27.952 --> 00:01:28.935
- I love this message.

00:01:28.935 --> 00:01:30.334
It's one of my favorite messages.

00:01:30.334 --> 00:01:32.810
I 100% agree with Jeff
on this one, and I think

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:36.183
you need to be insanely
stubborn about the mission,

00:01:36.183 --> 00:01:38.727
insanely stubborn about the
why you're doing things,

00:01:38.727 --> 00:01:41.564
but really flexible about the how.

00:01:41.564 --> 00:01:43.867
And I think you need to
have that stubbornness,

00:01:43.867 --> 00:01:45.465
especially as an entrepreneur,
because when you're

00:01:45.465 --> 00:01:49.502
getting started, you're going
to get so much pushback.

00:01:49.502 --> 00:01:51.689
What you create, your product,
your service, won't be

00:01:51.689 --> 00:01:54.155
really great at the start,
and so, it will be hard to get

00:01:54.155 --> 00:01:55.505
people to buy from you.

00:01:55.505 --> 00:02:00.099
You'll have people around you,
friends, family, co-workers,

00:02:00.099 --> 00:02:01.619
people in your community
telling you that it's

00:02:01.619 --> 00:02:02.851
not going to work out.

00:02:02.851 --> 00:02:05.551
You're telling yourself
that sometimes this is crazy

00:02:05.551 --> 00:02:06.790
and it's not going to work out.

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:10.767
And so everything around you
is saying that this is crazy,

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:13.688
and that maybe it's not the
smartest thing to do, right?

00:02:13.688 --> 00:02:16.002
Being an entrepreneur is
really the smart thing to do.

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:18.877
It might be the best thing
to do, but what we do is

00:02:18.877 --> 00:02:21.298
we create a world that does not exist.

00:02:21.298 --> 00:02:23.737
The best entrepreneurs
have a vision for a world

00:02:23.737 --> 00:02:26.977
that they want to create
that doesn't exist yet.

00:02:26.977 --> 00:02:30.101
So, from a practical perspective,
it doesn't make sense.

00:02:30.101 --> 00:02:32.529
We're doing something that
has never been done before.

00:02:32.529 --> 00:02:34.537
You guys need to be doing
something that's never

00:02:34.537 --> 00:02:36.401
been done before, right?

00:02:36.401 --> 00:02:38.499
You can model some success,
but at some point you have

00:02:38.499 --> 00:02:39.933
to find your own path.

00:02:39.933 --> 00:02:43.162
And when you go and create your own path,

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:45.096
that's not practical,
that's not logical because

00:02:45.096 --> 00:02:46.788
it doesn't exist yet.

00:02:46.788 --> 00:02:48.141
You have to go and create it.

00:02:48.141 --> 00:02:51.499
And so you need to have that
stubbornness for the mission,

00:02:51.499 --> 00:02:54.254
for the vision, for what end objective

00:02:54.254 --> 00:02:56.195
you're trying to create,

00:02:56.195 --> 00:02:58.778
because of all the pushback and negativity

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:00.702
and zero progress you're going to make

00:03:00.702 --> 00:03:01.849
at the beginning.

00:03:01.849 --> 00:03:03.964
If you don't have that stubbornness,

00:03:03.964 --> 00:03:05.447
if you aren't willing to say,

00:03:05.447 --> 00:03:08.311
"no, this is going to
work out", to yourself and

00:03:08.311 --> 00:03:10.854
to the people around
you who are naysayers,

00:03:10.854 --> 00:03:12.675
then you're going to quit.

00:03:12.675 --> 00:03:14.178
Which most entrepreneurs end up doing.

00:03:14.178 --> 00:03:16.110
They quit, they don't
have enough stubbornness

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:17.992
for where they want to go.

00:03:17.992 --> 00:03:18.825
The flexibility though,
is about how go out

00:03:18.825 --> 00:03:20.987
and accomplish it.

00:03:20.987 --> 00:03:22.993
I want to make this world better.

00:03:22.993 --> 00:03:24.343
Here is how I want it to look like.

00:03:24.343 --> 00:03:26.968
Here's what I want to
change in the industry.

00:03:26.968 --> 00:03:30.539
But how you go out and
do it should be flexible.

00:03:30.539 --> 00:03:32.551
And this is where, I think,
too many entrepreneurs

00:03:32.551 --> 00:03:34.277
are too stubborn.

00:03:34.277 --> 00:03:37.606
It has to be this specific
way and this way only.

00:03:37.606 --> 00:03:39.783
So you spend all this time
making this perfect plan,

00:03:39.783 --> 00:03:42.252
the perfectionist, you want
to make this perfect plan,

00:03:42.252 --> 00:03:44.060
and all your time is working on this plan,

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:46.641
and this is exactly how
it's going to play out.

00:03:46.641 --> 00:03:48.110
No matter how much planning you do,

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:50.501
it's never going to go
according to that plan.

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:52.961
Every successful business,
look at how they started,

00:03:52.961 --> 00:03:54.849
it's not how they started that led them

00:03:54.849 --> 00:03:56.611
to their ultimate success.

00:03:56.611 --> 00:03:59.292
Sometimes it's a radical
shift in their plan, sometimes

00:03:59.292 --> 00:04:01.054
it's a minor shift in their plan.

00:04:01.054 --> 00:04:03.435
But it always has to change.

00:04:03.435 --> 00:04:05.402
Just look at any company.

00:04:05.402 --> 00:04:07.120
Look at how they started,
look at Starbucks.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:08.512
They started selling just beans.

00:04:08.512 --> 00:04:10.475
You couldn't get coffee
going into a Starbucks.

00:04:10.475 --> 00:04:12.011
They would only sell you the beans.

00:04:12.011 --> 00:04:14.596
BMW started selling airplanes.

00:04:14.596 --> 00:04:16.937
It's why their logo is
an airplane propeller.

00:04:16.937 --> 00:04:19.433
Wrigley's, the gum company,
started selling other

00:04:19.433 --> 00:04:21.480
household products, and
gum was was just used

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:22.625
as a giveaway.

00:04:22.625 --> 00:04:25.243
That if you buy X packs
of this other product,

00:04:25.243 --> 00:04:26.847
we'll give you some gum.

00:04:26.847 --> 00:04:29.025
And they eventually
became the gum company.

00:04:29.025 --> 00:04:31.697
It changes so often, and
too many entrepreneurs

00:04:31.697 --> 00:04:32.530
are stuck on that it has
to be this specific way.

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:36.078
And if you're not listening
to the market, if you're not

00:04:36.078 --> 00:04:38.416
combining what you love
with what the market wants,

00:04:38.416 --> 00:04:40.797
you're never going to get to
the success that you're after.

00:04:40.797 --> 00:04:43.755
And so that insane
stubbornness for the vision

00:04:43.755 --> 00:04:46.542
but total flexibility for
how you accomplish it,

00:04:46.542 --> 00:04:48.753
that's what's really
important as an entrepreneur.

00:04:48.753 --> 00:04:51.276
If I look at my mission,
what I'm trying to do here,

00:04:51.276 --> 00:04:53.553
I want to help a billion entrepreneurs.

00:04:53.553 --> 00:04:55.573
I feel I have the potential to do it.

00:04:55.573 --> 00:04:58.719
I want to do it because,
on a one on one level

00:04:58.719 --> 00:05:01.769
it's just fulfilling to know
that what I do is meaningful,

00:05:01.769 --> 00:05:03.987
that I have an impact,
that I wake up daily and

00:05:03.987 --> 00:05:06.439
I get to do something that
impacts somebody else's life.

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:07.934
That means something to me.

00:05:07.934 --> 00:05:10.642
Seeing your comments come in
every day fills up my soul,

00:05:10.642 --> 00:05:13.857
knowing that I put work
out there, and it's being

00:05:13.857 --> 00:05:16.740
received well and it's having
an impact on your lives.

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:18.056
That means a lot to me.

00:05:18.056 --> 00:05:20.772
On a big scale, I think
entrepreneurs are going to solve

00:05:20.772 --> 00:05:22.324
all the problems of the world.

00:05:22.324 --> 00:05:24.207
It's not companies, it's not corporations,

00:05:24.207 --> 00:05:25.354
it's not government, it's us.

00:05:25.354 --> 00:05:26.211
We're going to solve it.

00:05:26.211 --> 00:05:29.008
And if I can help a billion
entrepreneurs do something

00:05:29.008 --> 00:05:32.201
greater in their companies
to help solve real problems,

00:05:32.201 --> 00:05:33.970
that's a major impact I've had.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:37.953
And so having half a
percent impact on your life,

00:05:37.953 --> 00:05:41.367
makes me feel like I'm having
a huge impact on the world.

00:05:41.367 --> 00:05:43.297
And that's what I set out to do.

00:05:43.297 --> 00:05:45.672
A lot of you guys see me
as YouTuber, and I've said

00:05:45.672 --> 00:05:48.086
many times, I'm not addicted to YouTube.

00:05:48.086 --> 00:05:51.787
I see YouTube as the best
platform right now, for someone

00:05:51.787 --> 00:05:55.357
like me, to spread my
message to someone like you.

00:05:55.357 --> 00:05:57.898
So it's the best path for me on my mission

00:05:57.898 --> 00:05:59.827
to achieve my big goal.

00:05:59.827 --> 00:06:00.890
But that may change.

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:03.478
And I anticipate that it will change.

00:06:03.478 --> 00:06:06.768
YouTube will not be the big
player probably in ten years.

00:06:06.768 --> 00:06:08.827
So what's the thing that's
going to come along that will

00:06:08.827 --> 00:06:11.975
replace YouTube that I have to jump in on,

00:06:11.975 --> 00:06:13.331
because I'm going to hit my goal.

00:06:13.331 --> 00:06:14.650
I want to have that impact.

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:17.725
And so even the types of
videos, so that's on a macro

00:06:17.725 --> 00:06:19.523
of the main strategy.

00:06:19.523 --> 00:06:23.395
The main strategy is YouTube,
endbook, and website,

00:06:23.395 --> 00:06:25.155
and that will change in the
future, but even the micro

00:06:25.155 --> 00:06:27.902
strategy within YouTube, okay,
so YouTube is one of the main

00:06:27.902 --> 00:06:31.794
strategies, micro strategy,
Believe Life series,

00:06:31.794 --> 00:06:33.437
Top Ten series, Meant to Me series,

00:06:33.437 --> 00:06:35.486
Entspresso series, Seven Way series,

00:06:35.486 --> 00:06:37.267
those are constantly in flux.

00:06:37.267 --> 00:06:39.544
What's working, what's having
an impact, what's helping us

00:06:39.544 --> 00:06:41.388
achieve our mission, and which ones are

00:06:41.388 --> 00:06:43.945
hurting the channel, or just
stagnating, that we know

00:06:43.945 --> 00:06:47.045
that we need to eliminate
and bring something else in.

00:06:47.045 --> 00:06:49.844
So not being so attached,
and say, this is a series,

00:06:49.844 --> 00:06:53.130
that even if it doesn't
work, I still have to do it.

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:54.990
This is the only series
that's going to work.

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:58.581
If I was like that, then we
wouldn't be having the impact

00:06:58.581 --> 00:06:59.653
that we have right now.

00:06:59.653 --> 00:07:01.131
It doesn't help me further my mission.

00:07:01.131 --> 00:07:02.897
And so I think, too often,

00:07:02.897 --> 00:07:05.175
entrepreneurs who start businesses

00:07:05.175 --> 00:07:07.164
are not stubborn enough
about where they want to go,

00:07:07.164 --> 00:07:09.675
about the mission vision, and
they end up quitting too soon.

00:07:09.675 --> 00:07:12.575
And they're too stubborn about
how they go out and execute

00:07:12.575 --> 00:07:15.490
their plan, and they're not
open enough to other feedback

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:18.318
to say, hey, I want to help
you get that mission to happen,

00:07:18.318 --> 00:07:20.003
here's another way way to
be able to go out and do it.

00:07:20.003 --> 00:07:22.128
So the question of the
day today is, I'm curious,

00:07:22.128 --> 00:07:24.028
what is something that
you've had to change about

00:07:24.028 --> 00:07:25.750
your plan, since getting started.

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:27.605
You went out with this
plan, and you realized that

00:07:27.605 --> 00:07:29.820
something didn't work, and
you had to make an adjustment

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:31.292
that then ended up working for you.

00:07:31.292 --> 00:07:32.319
What was that change?

00:07:32.319 --> 00:07:34.740
What changing your plan, that
little tweak that you made,

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:35.647
how did it work.

00:07:35.647 --> 00:07:37.578
I'd love to hear from you
down in the comments below,

00:07:37.578 --> 00:07:39.144
and I think it could help the
other entrepreneurs watching

00:07:39.144 --> 00:07:40.003
as well.

00:07:40.003 --> 00:07:41.917
And, if you leave a comment
within the first couple

00:07:41.917 --> 00:07:43.256
hours of this video going live,

00:07:43.256 --> 00:07:45.878
you have a chance to win
one of our two daily prizes.

00:07:45.878 --> 00:07:47.904
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Mike Lamothe from

00:07:47.904 --> 00:07:49.129
ChartYourTrade.com.

00:07:49.129 --> 00:07:51.516
Mike, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:07:51.516 --> 00:07:52.381
Your One Word.

00:07:52.381 --> 00:07:54.149
It really, really means a lot to me, man,

00:07:54.149 --> 00:07:55.789
and I hope you enjoyed the read.

00:07:55.789 --> 00:07:57.056
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:07:57.056 --> 00:07:58.173
I believe in you.

00:07:58.173 --> 00:08:01.006
I hope you continue to believe
in yourself and whatever

00:08:01.006 --> 00:08:05.173
Your One Word is, much
love, and I'll see you again

